From ca93109ec0d9c921900549016090d97aed9831cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:04:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Make the pre-battle bust match the picked model

The connection screen's close-up never consults the model switch the battle
scene uses -- community review established the bust is a full-model render,
and disassembly found its actual selector: a save-class mapper (game plus
gender, six classes) indexing two widget-id tables in DOL data. So battles
showed the picked model while the bust stubbornly showed the protagonist.

The code block now also remaps the bust: each side's save-class entry in both
tables is pointed at the picked model's class widget. An exhaustive reach
audit proved the tables are read only by the connection menu and written by
nothing, so the remap is cosmetic and uncontested. Honest limits, from the
menu's own contents: only the six GBA player models have bust widgets, so an
arbitrary-model pick keeps the vanilla bust while the battle model still
changes; and when both saves share a class the two sides would fight over one
table entry, so the remap stands down entirely.

Version 1.3.4.
